  "notes": "Best configuration found by scripts/km_margin.py plus a closed-loop sweep, validated on both physics engines. Flat front-jet brackets (the CAD's FRONT_JET_TILT30 replaced by straight mounts), hover pitch 26.0 deg, centre of gravity exactly as the CAD gives it. Tolerates a reaction-torque coefficient up to 0.008 against 0.002 as built, holds position five times tighter, and runs the motors cooler. Moving the centre of gravity scores better on a static allocation check and is worse in flight: see the commit that added this file."
